WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Adult retinas and dogs rewired themselves after single-dose gene therapy, rebuilding damaged connections and recovering vision. This is Planetarian Daily, episode 197. Researchers at Michigan State University College of Veterinary Medicine tested CABP4 gene therapy in adult dogs with an inherited condition that disrupts calcium signaling between light sensing cells and the brain. The single-dose treatment prompted mature retinal cells to rebuild

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.080
damaged connections. Retina's thickened and visual function recovered. Three

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:39.400
independent structural changes supported plasticity in fully developed tissue.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:44.160
Pre-existing abnormalities were repaired in addition to new components being

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.880
added. Dogs with spontaneous disease served as a model for human childhood

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:53.640
blindness. Billy Beckwith Cohen compared the therapy to an editor supplying

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:58.440
corrected instructions for a blueprint typo. Mature mammalian nerve cells

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:02.200
rebuild connections and repaired abnormalities after a single dose.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:06.560
The extent of physical restoration in adult tissue surprised the team.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:11.840
Beckwith Cohen noted that the therapy supplied corrected instructions like an editor fixing

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:12.960
a blueprint typo.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:19.300
What remains unclear is how widely this plasticity applies across other inherited retinal conditions.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.800
Now shifting to imaging tools.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:27.400
Kyushu University researchers developed a water soluble version of the luminescent organic

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:34.360
radical Trist2,4,6 trichlorophenyl methyl. The molecule produces fluorescence while serving

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:40.340
as an MRI-contrast agent without paramagnetic metals. Optimization improved both water

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:45.200
solubility and fluorescence activity after earlier versions showed weak fluorescence.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:51.180
The approach avoids potential side effects linked to gadolinium agents. Associate Professor

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:55.340
Ken Albrecht led the work at the Institute for Materials Chemistry and Engineering.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:02:05.040
On a different note, ecologist Rosa Boone showed that fungi and bacteria responsible for soil odor can be captured and analyzed in the lab.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:10.440
The work supports development of an electronic nose sensor for direct microbial assessment.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.620
Monitoring gains importance ahead of new soil monitoring guidelines.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:20.180
Boone noted that the fungi and bacteria present in the soil are important for soil health.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:26.300
Next up, environmental disturbance from the 2011 tsunami brought previously separated

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.920
fish species into contact.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:32.660
Hybridization occurred, yet species boundaries largely remained intact.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.300
The findings address how species limits persist amid habitat change.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:43.260
The study examined how species boundaries are maintained in the face of environmental disturbance.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:48.800
Researchers tested whether bolting initial letters guides eye-focus and lets the brain

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:54.440
complete words. The method produced no measurable improvement in reading speed or understanding.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:03:00.740
The idea is that guiding the eyes to focus on highlighted initial letters lets the brain complete the word.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:08.860
Leibnitz Center for Agricultural Landscape Research measured soil changes during installation of combined solar and farming systems.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:13.580
The study provides the first data on how construction phases alter soil.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:18.520
Researcher's examines soil protection measures in agri-photovoltaics.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:24.320
Psychologists Steve Stewart-Williams examines three questions on how evolution shaped male

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:25.420
and female minds.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:29.880
The work draws on and is sometimes distorted by online communities.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:35.520
The book is titled A Billion Years of Sex Differences, How Evolution Shaped the Minds

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:36.400
of Men and Women.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:42.180
Industrial wastewater from textiles and other sectors releases stable synthetic dyes.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:47.980
Researchers turned bull rush into a copper-enhanced adsorbent that removes dyes from water.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:53.200
The material targets synthetic dyes that are chemically stable and difficult to biodegrade.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:59.980
A large health record analysis linked glucosamine intake to a 25% higher chance of mild

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:02.400
cognitive impairment advancing to dementia.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:08.420
Laboratory experiments indicated the supplement may intensify abnormal sugar tagging in the

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:09.300
Alzheimer's brain.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:14.840
clinical trials are still required to confirm causation. The analysis examined

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:20.180
progression from mild cognitive impairment to dementia. DNA analysis revealed

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:25.540
chemosynthesis genes in bacteria living on fish gills. The microbiome appears

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:30.660
specialized and may influence fish metabolism and immunity. The presence in fish

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:35.860
appears to be a new discovery. Pain and fatigue continue after inflammation control

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:42.040
in rheumatoid arthritis. Depression, poor sleep, obesity, smoking, and chronic pain may

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:47.580
sustain symptoms. Identifying these drivers could avoid unnecessary medication changes.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:52.800
Researchers examined why pain persists even when inflammation is under control.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:58.780
Samples collected along the state coastline contain compounds with possible applications in cancer

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:04.920
treatment and cosmetics. The algae were found on the state's coast. The Nobel-winning work on water

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:08.900
channels emerged from unexpected observations during routine experiments.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:12.140
The discovery involved collaboration and chance.

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:17.900
Patients with hard-to-treat lipid disorders received one dose of experimental CRISPR therapy.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:25.340
LDL fell by 52.5% and triglycerides by 47.8% at the highest dose.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.320
Reductions remained at the 12-month mark.

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:31.620
The therapy targets difficult-to-treat lipid disorders.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:38.140
factors. After tracing ancient cellular conditions, more than 12,000 fossils from early eukaryotes

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:43.780
were recovered from Australian rocks. Complex cells appeared only in oxygen-rich settings,

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:50.020
while simpler microbes occupied oxygen-free zones. The findings strengthen the idea that oxygen

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:55.440
played a crucial role in the emergence of complex life. Most people assume the body simply

00:05:55.440 --> 00:06:00.700
sweats to cool down when temperatures rise. In reality, right now, your skin blood vessels

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:06.080
are widening to release heat, while sweat glands activate in coordinated waves across different

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:12.160
body regions. A single square meter of skin can evaporate roughly one liter of sweat per hour

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:17.040
under peak conditions, moving heat away far more efficiently than radiation alone.

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:22.640
The process begins in the hypothalamus, which compares core temperature against a set point

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:28.260
and sends signals through the autonomic nervous system. When humidity blocks evaporation,

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:32.600
the same system ramps up heart rate to push more blood toward the skin surface.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:37.800
One practical step is to watch for early signs of heat strain, such as sudden fatigue

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:42.700
or dizziness during routine activity, rather than waiting for obvious overheating.

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:48.280
Keep an eye on follow-up data from ongoing CRISPR lipid trials expected in coming months.

